# Reserved DOS device names. A tool running `> NUL` (or `2> NUL`, `*> NUL`) inside
# the source dir under a POSIX shell writes a literal file by that name instead of
# discarding output, which Windows tooling that assumes cmd.exe semantics does.
# chezmoi would then try to manage a target of the same name, whose bare path
# resolves to the character device, aborting the whole apply. These are never real
# managed targets, so ignore them on every OS.
